  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (0001_PL_001, 0001_PL_002, 0001_PL_100, 0001_PL_101, 0001_PL_102, 0001_PL_103,  0001_PL_104, 0001_PL_105, 0001_PL_106, 0001_PL_110, 0001_PL_111, 0001_PL_112, 0001_PL_113, 0001_PL_114, 0001_PL_115, 0001_PL_116, 0001_PL_120, 0001_PL_122, 0001_PL_123, 0001_PL_124, 0001_PL_125, 0001_PL_126, 0001_PL_127, sustainable drainage assessment, structural methodology statement, Design and access statement- received 18/02/2022) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am  to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 9 :00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - No development shall be carried out until such time as the person carrying out the work is a member of the Considerate Constructors Scheme and its code of practice, and the details of the membership and contact details are clearly displayed on the site so that they can be easily read by members of the public.",
    "Condition : 6 - The basement hereby permitted shall at no time be used or occupied as a separate dwelling independent of the main house and shall not be used as sleeping accommodation.",
    "Condition : 7 - Prior to first occupation, evidence (schedule of installed fittings and\nmanufactures literature) shall be submitted to and approved in writing\nby the Local Planning Authority to demonstrate that the development\nhas achieved an internal water use of 105L/person/day or less.\nMeasures integrated shall be retained for the lifetime of the\ndevelopment."
  ],
